 
  He did not open it that night. He set it on the mantel above the
  stove in the keeper's kitchen and looked at it through supper. He
  looked at it while he wound the clockwork that still turned the
  lens on nights when the generator was being stubborn, and again
  while he wrote the log: [0m[3mWind SW 5, sea moderate, visibility good. [0m
  [0m[3mLight exhibited 18:42.[0m He looked at it in the morning.

  On the third night he opened it. 
 
  [0m[3mDear Catriona,[0m it began, in a careful, slanting hand. [0m[3mThe mail boat[0m
  [0m[3mhas not come for two weeks on account of the weather and I have [0m
  [0m[3mbegun to think it will never come again and that you will think I [0m
  [0m[3mhave forgotten you. I have not forgotten you. I think of nothing [0m
  [0m[3melse. If you will have me, I will come out to Fennick at the spring[0m
  [0m[3mterm and I will teach the little ones their sums while you teach [0m
  [0m[3mthem their letters, and we will grow old in that schoolhouse [0m
  [0m[3mtogether and never speak of the mainland again. Please say yes. [0m
  [0m[3mWrite to me at the post office in Oban. — Robert.[0m
 
  Elias read it four times. Then he put it back in its envelope and
  returned it to the mantel. He found, to his considerable surprise,
  that he wanted very badly to know what Catriona Bell had said.

  ---
 
  After that he began to look.
  
  He was not sure what he was looking for at first. He walked the
  rock at low tide and searched the wrack line where weed, timber and
  plastic collected in the clefts. He asked Dougie and the other
  boatmen to bring him anything that looked like paper. He wrote to
  the postmaster in Oban, a patient young woman named Isla Grant, and
  asked whether the post office ever kept mail it couldn't deliver.
 
  Isla wrote back that the old sorting office had a cupboard full of
  it. Nobody had wanted to burn it, and nobody had known what else to
  do. [0m[3mIf you're serious,[0m she wrote, *I'll send it out. It's taking
